course: dictionary
lesson: 1870
title: Feelings in a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «She looked at him coldly and said nothing.» Coldly does not mean the room was chilly. It means in an unfriendly way, without warmth or kindness.
explain: The clues are "looked at him" and "said nothing": nobody is smiling and nobody is being friendly. Try the swap check: "She looked at him unkindly and said nothing" still makes sense, so coldly means unkindly here.
explain: Coldly is about feelings, not temperature. Phrases like «replied coldly» and «coldly polite» show someone being distant or angry. Coldly polite means polite on the outside but not warm on the inside.
fact: Coldly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, such as looked, replied or stared.
fact: «Coldly» means in an unfriendly way, without warmth or kindness.
fact: «Coldly» describes feelings, not temperature. A room can be cold, but a person can look or speak coldly.
fact: Good phrases to notice are «replied coldly», «stared coldly» and «coldly polite».
fact: The same word can change its meaning with the feeling behind it: «tǎoyàn!» (Chinese) said laughing means "stop it, you!", but said coldly it shows real dislike.
exercise: «She stared at him coldly across the table.» What does coldly tell you about her? | She was singing happily | She felt chilly and needed a coat | She was very tired | *She was unfriendly towards him
exercise: «He replied coldly, without even looking up.» Find the word that tells you how he replied. | *coldly | without | looking | replied
exercise: Which phrase shows someone who is polite on the outside but not warm on the inside? | *coldly polite | cold weather | happily sad | warm and cheerful greeting
test: «The waiter bowed coldly and said, "Your table is not ready."» What does coldly mean here? | *In an unfriendly way, without warmth | Very quickly | Happily, with a big smile | Because the room was cold
test: Which sentence uses coldly to show an unfriendly feeling? | The ice cream was coldly sweet | *He answered her coldly, and then turned away | The river ran coldly under the bridge | The weather was coldly wet
exam: Jayden reads «Her goodbye was cold and polite» and says coldly means the room was chilly. Is he right? | No, it means she was late | *No, coldly is about feelings, so it means unfriendly | Yes, it means the room was cold | Yes, it means she was shivering
